"""Checked secure entropy from the existing synchronous crypto owners.

`sosix_random_hex(n)`: None denotes provider failure or malformed entropy;
callers must fail closed. The length is a byte count, so 16 requests 32
hexadecimal characters. The hex text is immutable and cannot be wiped.

`sosix_random_bytes(n)`: exactly `n` OS CSPRNG bytes as a `[u8]` the caller
owns and can wipe, or Err on provider failure, a zero request or a request over
1 MiB (`entropy_platform_bytes` over `rt_entropy_fill`). Use it for secrets.
"""
export use std.nogc_sync_mut.io.crypto_sffi.{random_hex as sosix_random_hex}
export use std.nogc_sync_mut.crypto.entropy_platform.{entropy_platform_bytes as sosix_random_bytes}
